#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106643} :activity/id #uuid "e068c66e-c6f9-5b98-88d1-321d4bd52ecb" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050650 :topic/id #uuid "5c5917ee-8504-5c4f-8c53-d54f4a7e936f" :topic/math-academy-id 1321} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106643 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107162 :tutorial/content "Consider the polygon $ABCD$, where the side $\\overline{AB}$ is extended beyond the vertex $B.$\n\n![](images/fa/fa23c036920e2c506c38f1e7be8a498c0a349ef145e8c444201665345bc648e4.png)\n\nWe call $\\color{blue}\\angle{CBE}$ the **exterior angle** of the vertex $B$.\n\nGiven a polygon's vertex, the interior and exterior angles are supplementary. So, for the vertex $B,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\color{YellowOrange}m\\angle{ABC}}_{\\large\\text{Interior}} \\:+\\: \\underbrace{\\color{blue}m\\angle{CBE}}_{\\large\\text{Exterior}} = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nWe have the following theorem:\n\nThe measures of the exterior angles of any simple polygon sum to $360^\\circ.$\n\nWe'll show why this theorem is true at the end of the lesson.\n\nLet's label the exterior angles of our polygon below:\n\n![](images/ac/acc0ac90f27a78e83b6b14651f61ddfe6a87afa56b6e51a1af57f5e74c31689f.png)\n\nAccording to our theorem, these four angles sum to $360^\\circ.$\n\n$$\na+b+c+d = 360^\\circ\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "6cb4a5ba-6c28-59e2-ab72-89e4f5f69ae3" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8041 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "4bf926eb-9821-545f-b67e-d2d50c4f61f0" :step/math-academy-id 187128 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106644}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106644 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105749 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105471 :question/id #uuid "0cd03b60-baf3-5689-9f84-5f8be9853a9b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12838"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9846ca00-8305-56a8-a14d-7aa2488c0016" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048201}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106212} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506537} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506538}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Exterior Angles"} :step/id #uuid "2d241585-6a66-55ed-8dd4-a690566db2a8" :step/math-academy-id 187129 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106645}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106645 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105750 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105472 :question/id #uuid "fbc903e6-45ee-53c5-9d31-0edf8140cacd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12839"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5de9bf2f-b11c-5af0-a569-5f25aebae227" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048725}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106033} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106077} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506512} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518119}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Exterior Angles"} :step/id #uuid "80b138e7-13bc-505c-9c7b-e57531dd484d" :step/math-academy-id 187132 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106646}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106646 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105751 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105473 :question/id #uuid "44ea9915-91ca-5abf-a1ac-bb801069ef24" :question/math-academy-id "e-12879"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0794b384-c2ff-5d4a-b325-28077b5b1f96" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048673} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050452}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106199} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106390} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506556} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506557} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518185} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518209}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Quantity Using Exterior Angles"} :step/id #uuid "c27f1faa-2fca-5dc4-8283-8cf462884593" :step/math-academy-id 187135 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106647}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106647 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105752 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105474 :question/id #uuid "e96a16e9-122f-582c-beb9-22ca0d4d7d68" :question/math-academy-id "e-12880"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64712488-234f-5d44-92a9-6a4821f2d304" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050127}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106078} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106488} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506562} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518110} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518205}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Exterior Angle by Determining an Unknown Quantity"} :step/id #uuid "f65fca30-a9ac-5101-b87a-1c01743c0b0b" :step/math-academy-id 187138 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106648}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106648 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107163 :tutorial/content "Why do the exterior angles of a polygon always sum to $360^\\circ?$\n\nSuppose we have an $n$-sided polygon. Then, we have the following:\n\n- There are $n$ pairs of interior-exterior angles, each pair being supplementary (i.e., their measures add to $180^\\circ).$\n\n- Therefore, the sum of the measures of *all* interior-exterior pairs equals ${\\color{blue}n\\cdot 180^\\circ}.$\n\n- In a previous lesson, we saw that the sum of the *interior* angles equals ${\\color{red}{(n-2)\\cdot 180^\\circ}}.$\n\nTherefore, to get the sum of the *exterior* angles, we subtract ${\\color{red}{(n-2)\\cdot 180^\\circ}}$ from ${\\color{blue}n\\cdot 180^\\circ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Sum of Exterior Angles} & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘}-(n-2)\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\  & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘}-n\\cdot {180}^{∘}+2\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\cancel{n\\cdot {180}^{∘}}-\\cancel{n\\cdot {180}^{∘}}+2\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis proves that the sum of the exterior angles of a (simple) polygon equals $360^\\circ.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "fb5a1532-47ec-5455-96c8-49187460e543" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8042 :tutorial/title "Proving the Theorem"} :step/id #uuid "ee786271-6101-5bf4-9d57-2fe763770d7a" :step/math-academy-id 187141}] :activity/title "Exterior Angles of Polygons" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105975}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518231} :activity/id #uuid "4642b563-78a1-574f-85b9-bdf648e97e49" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050650 :topic/id #uuid "5c5917ee-8504-5c4f-8c53-d54f4a7e936f" :topic/math-academy-id 1321} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518227 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6318460b-5678-5646-a910-82e6cf183480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517670}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517670} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cb61399-54db-53c5-9e53-bf360481e48d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2ac19296-c890-536b-9e9a-47b0cd74c840" :question/math-academy-id "q-223356" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e40dfd3842ec7a7b5de16d7938988e86209960ae9cba510bbac004b0bb73d94.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠B$ is{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let us call $x$ the exterior angle of $∠B.$ Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{58}^{∘}+x+{65}^{∘}+{63}^{∘}+{97}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x+{283}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={77}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0e3febc6-ffc1-5247-a54a-b79a2b1756e7"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518231 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95de501c-c29d-5cbf-9a79-048a79089948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517771}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517771} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7ff32db-e290-547d-9167-5bfd000c5b9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b40960a4-3462-5880-9ff6-2c1313bf33f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-171905" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bd6b42e1d48ca0e45ffc9b8910345bea52f1f44f9754f00ac4a4ba034e273bb5.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3x+(2x+{20}^{∘})+(5x-{24}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 14x-{4}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 14x & ={364}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={26}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "22c064e1-9b1b-5de4-87cd-f9e10b1b6ac9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518280}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518272 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a27d61-a734-57ce-a1b9-e6a9d52463e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{155}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517553} {:answer/id #uuid "9ccb46db-67ff-50b8-8b68-b38569111f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{168}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517791} {:answer/id #uuid "aefd51f3-7fe9-58df-9f1a-21094a7ee66a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{152}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517818} {:answer/id #uuid "df4121c9-1388-5799-80fd-0cbb19b668e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{173}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517909} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7972ee-be19-5bae-a8dd-d693c56fe478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{163}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517936}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517553} :answer-field/id #uuid "b89379c4-d191-53ca-8ac5-ec0071d31fd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "143c348d-4bc6-5a45-bf95-01d78dce959f" :question/math-academy-id "q-223201" :question/problem "![](images/33/33c1016cb2353e5332a5e04e8f377d4fa7d76e1b569a3532a45c5a068cc6d255.png)\n\nFor the quadrilateral above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6x+{23}^{∘})+(17x-{4}^{∘})+(21x+{8}^{∘})+(4x-{3}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 48x+{24}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 48x & ={336}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={7}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21x+{8}^{∘} & =21({7}^{∘})+{8}^{∘} \\\\  & ={147}^{∘}+8 \\\\  & ={155}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "91a10bad-5a62-55ff-aa9b-d76baf287c2f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518276}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518276 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518205 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b680264-dfb5-59a3-bcc8-c4eaa88b0281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517512}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517512} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7c212c7-8e24-558b-a30f-86787ad1fb45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "da26be71-f6d6-5898-b94d-3e43f1a50c61" :question/math-academy-id "q-223237" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c8bc8341b9619e9fddb151b02d2d859fab801fe35114de6b2ce6d09045fff11.png)\n\nFor the quadrilateral above, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ is{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the measure of the exterior angle at $B$ is ${180}^{∘}-(4x+{18}^{∘})={162}^{∘}-4x.$\n\nSince the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x+{15}^{∘})+({162}^{∘}-4x)+(4x-{2}^{∘})+(3x+{1}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{176}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={184}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={23}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-{2}^{∘} & =4({23}^{∘})-{2}^{∘} \\\\  & ={92}^{∘}-{2}^{∘} \\\\  & ={90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "98d8757a-5405-536c-b667-673b49141522" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518227}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518280 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e08b8587-2673-5d67-85be-e9c69a264b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517910}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517910} :answer-field/id #uuid "525a4469-4e3e-58b4-bc94-04e70a60046c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e54967a4-313f-5425-b80c-928ee57bb212" :question/math-academy-id "q-223198" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a92c3df4f9d410b1a7620cf43b04fda1ce7312cebd8c6077a0b0411ecc78ad73.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2x+(x+{10}^{∘})+(2x-{10}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 6x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a5175f00-0d37-5905-a6f9-12c953f10f27" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518272}}] :activity/title "Exterior Angles of Polygons" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517484}]}
